Package: nxd-qt6-compat
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Manuel Jesús Romero Mateos <manu4.2012@gmail.com>
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Depends: libqt6gui6 (>= 6.8.2), libqt6network6 (>= 6.8.2)
Provides: libqt6gui6t64 (= 6.8.2+nxd), libqt6network6t64 (= 6.8.2+nxd)
Homepage: https://github.com/manu-romero-411/nx-debian
Description: Debian on the Nintendo Switch: Ubuntu's names of two Qt 6 libraries
 Packages built for Ubuntu 24.04, like the moonlight-qt of the Moonlight
 project's L4T repository, ask for libqt6gui6t64 and libqt6network6t64: the
 names Ubuntu gives Qt 6.4. Debian 13's Qt 6.8 ships the same libraries
 (libQt6Gui.so.6, libQt6Network.so.6, which Qt 6 keeps binary compatible) as
 libqt6gui6 and libqt6network6. This package depends on those and provides
 the Ubuntu names, so such packages install and update with apt.
 .
 The names are provided as version 6.8.2+nxd: above every 6.8.2+dfsg-N of
 Debian 13, whose libqt6gui6 and libqt6network6 break the t64 packages below
 their own version.
